  "notes": "The intersection is derivable in closed form: the cylinder (axis at x=y=0, z[-10,40]) is strictly inside the box laterally (r20 < 30) and overshoots it vertically, so target ∩ tool is exactly a cylinder r20 with z[0,30] — the box planes cut the overshoot, nothing else. No tangency, no coplanar faces. Analytic derivation: volume = pi*20^2*30 = 12000*pi; surface = lateral + two caps = 2*pi*20*30 + 2*pi*20^2 = 2000*pi; center of mass (0,0,15). Topology verified against pinned OCCT V8_0_0_p1 and identical to the cylinder primitive: 3 faces (lateral with seam + two caps), 3 edges (two circles + seam line), 2 vertices (seam endpoints).",
